sentences.t:
Ἥφαιστ’, ἦ ἄρα δή τις, ὅσαι θεαί εἰσ’ ἐν Ὀλύμπῳ,
τοσσάδ’ ἐνὶ φρεσὶν ᾗσιν ἀνέσχετο κήδεα λυγρὰ
ὅσσ’ ἐμοὶ ἐκ πασέων Κρονίδης Ζεὺς ἄλγε’ ἔδωκεν;

sentences.tr:
Hēphaist’, ē ara dē tis, hosai theai eis’ en Olympōi,
tossad’ eni phresin hēisin anescheto kēdea lygra
hoss’ emoi ek paseōn Kronidēs Zeus alge’ edōken;

sentences.l:
Him I, having reared him like a plant on the rich ground of an orchard,
sent forth upon the curved ships into Ilium
to fight the Trojans;

but the Achaeans
the Trojans at the sterns were penning in, and outside
they would not let them go;

In the one there were weddings and banquets,
and brides out of their chambers under blazing torches
they were leading through the town, and loud the wedding-song had risen;

and there a quarrel
had arisen, and two men were quarrelling for the sake of the requital
for a man who had perished;

and the elders
were sitting on polished stones in a sacred circle,
and sceptres of the air-voiced heralds they held in their hands;
